istinction explicitly so a reviewer doesn't read it as inherited.\n\n## One observation I deliberately did *not* act on\n\n`fold_listing` separates entries with `b\"\\n\"`, so a work path containing a literal newline could spell a second entry and fold two different trees equal — the same defect class, reached by a crafted filename rather than an ordinary rename. I left it alone and wrote it into the fragment for an adjudicator: the module's stated bound is that it defeats *accident, not intent* (DECISION 3, owner-ruled), and changing the separator would shift every identity value on an already-closed lane. That's a ruling to make, not a fix for me to slip in.\n\n## Committed\n\n`66844228` — the verification record, ending with the `WI: WI-579` trailer. It touches only `docs/log.d/`, and I verified the consequence rather than assuming it: the governing identity is byte-identical (`0f33ef91…`) across the close, the telemetry commit, and mine — so it bought the lane **no additional review round**.\n\nWorking tree clean; the close ritual is intact (Deliverable before Context, `specref` cleared, spec in `docs/archive/work/complete/`, approval brief regenerates to a no-op). The lane now owes only its final verdict round — a reviewer's act on trunk, not mine to perform."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":118385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aaed8dad-1e17-4092-b855-9708c49f0dac","uuid":"820a6871-52de-437a-84d9-f0066db4a6bd","request_id":"req_011Ceg4jQvjddEkVDp1UWFmx"}
